:null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3939233710","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/113513#issuecomment-3939233710","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113513","id":3939233710,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7qy--u","user":{"login":"erodozer","id":316728,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxNjcyOA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/316728?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/erodozer","html_url":"https://github.com/erodozer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erodozer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erodozer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erodozer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erodozer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erodozer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erodozer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erodozer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erodozer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/erodozer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-21T18:46:18Z","updated_at":"2026-02-21T18:46:42Z","body":"This looks to be another use-case that could be fixed by #102366\n\nEffectively, all I need is to be able to use a custom blend mode of\n|func|src color|dst color|src alpha|dst alpha|\n|-|-|-|-|-|\n|GL_FUNC_ADD|GL_ONE|GL_ONE|GL_ONE|GL_ONE|","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3939233710/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4434608006","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/113513#issuecomment-4434608006","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113513","id":4434608006,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABCFK_hg","user":{"login":"stuckupfool","id":3372077,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMzNzIwNzc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3372077?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuckupfool","html_url":"https://github.com/stuckupfool","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuckupfool/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuckupfool/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuckupfool/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuckupfool/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuckupfool/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuckupfool/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuckupfool/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuckupfool/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuckupfool/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-12T20:41:09Z","updated_at":"2026-05-12T20:41:09Z","body":"I'm currently hitting a roadblock with Godot 4.6 due to this issue. My use case is basically the same as @erodozer has described above. I'm looking to use SubViewports to render multiple [influence maps](https://gamedev.net/tutorials/programming/artificial-intelligence/the-core-mechanics-of-influence-mapping-r2799/) as a single packed texture that are then referenced by various game mechanics and AI agents in my game to make decisions. These maps require basic addition/subtraction operations to heat and cool each channel of the packed texture, however the current `blend_add` and `blend_sub` blending modes are unusable for this due to the alpha pre-multiplication. As a workaround I am forced to utilize only 3 channels per texture which limits the total number of influence maps my game can utilize simultaneously.\n\n@AThousandShips Is there anyway to approach this topic with the rendering dev team and push this forward? There's currently two open PRs that solve the problem with different styles of exposing the underlying functionality:\n- [#116686](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/116686)\n- [#102366](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102366)\nBoth seem to be perfectly fine solutions from a purely technical standpoint, so it seems like a bit of a shame that this is stuck in limbo because we can't agree on how to surface these options.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4434608006/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4434879885","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/113513#issuecomment-4434879885","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113513","id":4434879885,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABCFbljQ","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.